  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45712\", \"PowerToys#23857\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. PowerToys#45712 describes the same problem: with the taskbar on the left or top, the Quick Access popup still opens in the bottom-right corner instead of next to the tray icon, and the reporter suggests either auto-detecting the tray position or adding a setting to choose the corner. That ticket has no fix or workaround recorded in the archive. PowerToys#23857 is an earlier report of the same behavior, which was marked as a duplicate and expected to be fixed in a hotfix, but the later report shows the popup still ignores the taskbar position. In the meantime, the only option suggested is to open Quick Access with a global shortcut instead of the tray icon, and to add your vote or details to PowerToys#45712.\"}",
